{
  "text": "In paper  , a representation of the (p, q)-outer generalized inverse based on (1, 5) inverse over Banach algebra is presented . But as in our introduction in this paper, we indicate that Theorem 1.4 of  is wrong. We have to say that Theorem 2.1 in  is also wrong since the proof mainly based on  Theorem 1.4] . In fact, Theorem 2.1 in  gives the representation of a (1) a (2,l) p,q exists; (2) (aw)   exists and K r (a) \u2229 R r (w) = {0}; (3) (wa)   exists and R r (w) = R r (wa).",
